1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,080
Good morning, my name is Erica Matthews

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:09,917
and I'm the owner of Matthews Island Holidays,

3
00:00:09,917 --> 00:00:14,000
a company set up by my parents.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,340
Thank you for coming to this presentation

5
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:20,450
in which I hope to interest you in what we have to offer.

6
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:23,120
We're a small family-run company

7
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:26,512
and we believe in the importance of the personal touch,

8
00:00:26,512 --> 00:00:32,170
so we don't aim to compete with other companies on the number of customers.

9
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:36,140
What we do is build on our many years' experience

10
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:39,560
more than almost any other rail holiday company

11
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:42,775
to ensure we provide perfect holidays

12
00:00:42,775 --> 00:00:48,520
and a small number of destinations which we've got to know extremely well.

13
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:52,290
I'll start with our 6-day Isle of Man holiday.

14
00:00:52,290 --> 00:00:55,742
This is a fascinating island in the Irish sea,

15
00:00:55,742 --> 00:00:59,060
with Wales to the south, England to the east

16
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:03,030
Scotland to the north, and Northern Ireland to the west.

17
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:05,032
Our holiday starts in Hashim,

18
00:01:05,032 --> 00:01:08,460
where your tour manager will meet you

19
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:11,840
then you'll travel by ferry to the Isle of Man.

20
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:14,646
Some people prefer to fly from Luton instead

21
00:01:14,646 --> 00:01:18,360
and another popular option is to go by train to Liverpool

22
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:20,610
and take a ferry from there.

23
00:01:20,610 --> 00:01:23,450
You have 5 nights in the hotel

24
00:01:23,450 --> 00:01:26,840
and the price covers 5 breakfast and dinners

25
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:31,160
and lunch on the 3 days when there are organized trips.

26
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:37,390
Day 4 is free and most people have lunch in a cafe or restaurant in Douglas.

27
00:01:37,390 --> 00:01:42,195
The price of the holiday includes the ferry to the Isle of Man,

28
00:01:42,195 --> 00:01:46,630
all travel on the island, the hotel and the meals I've mentioned.

29
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:52,100
Incidentally, we tried to make booking our holidays as simple and fair as possible.

30
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:53,966
So, unlike with many companies,

31
00:01:53,966 --> 00:02:00,310
the price is the same whether you book six months in advance or at the last minute.

32
00:02:00,310 --> 00:02:04,050
And there's no supplement for single rooms in hotels.

33
00:02:04,050 --> 00:02:07,580
If you make a booking, then need to change the start date

34
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,440
for example because of illness.

35
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:15,940
You're welcome to change to an alternative date to a different tour for a small administrative fee.

36
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:19,990
Okay, so what does the holiday consist of?

37
00:02:19,990 --> 00:02:26,143
Well on Day 1, you'll arrive in time for a short introduction by your tour manager,

38
00:02:26,143 --> 00:02:28,450
followed by dinner in the hotel.

39
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:34,070
The dining room looks out at the river close to where it flows into the harbour,

40
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:36,880
and there's usually plenty of activity going on.

41
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:41,360
On Day 2, you'll take the coach to the small town of peel

42
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:45,530
on the way calling in at the Tynwald Exhibition.

43
00:02:45,530 --> 00:02:48,800
The Isle of Man isn't part of the United Kingdom

44
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:52,810
and it has its own parliament called Tynwald.

45
00:02:52,810 --> 00:02:57,820
It's claimed that this is the world's oldest parliament that's still functioning

46
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:01,590
and that it dates back to 979.

47
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:07,620
However, the earliest surviving reference to it is from 1422.

48
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:12,000
So perhaps it isn't quite as old as it claims.

49
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,500
Day 3, we have a trip to the Mountain Snaefell.

50
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:22,990
This begins with a leisurely ride along the promenade in Douglas in a horse-drawn tram.

51
00:03:22,990 --> 00:03:29,190
Then you board an electric train which takes you to the fishing village of Laxey.

52
00:03:29,190 --> 00:03:35,990
From there it's an 8km ride in the Snaefell Mountain railway to the top.

53
00:03:35,990 --> 00:03:41,880
Lunch will be in a cafe giving you spectacular views of the island.

54
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:47,399
Day 4 is free for you to explore, using the pass which will give you,

55
00:03:47,399 --> 00:03:54,390
so you won't have to pay for travel on local transport or for entrance to the island's heritage sites.

56
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:57,220
Or you might just want to take it easy in Douglas

57
00:03:57,220 --> 00:04:00,350
and perhaps do a little light shopping.

58
00:04:00,350 --> 00:04:04,970
The last full day, Day 5 is for some people.

59
00:04:04,970 --> 00:04:12,090
The highlight of the holiday was a ride on the steam railway from Douglas to port Erin.

60
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:13,936
After some time to explore,

61
00:04:13,936 --> 00:04:18,520
a coach will take you to the headland that overlooks the Calf of Man

62
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:21,690
a small island just off the coast.

63
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:24,305
From there, you continue to castle town

64
00:04:24,305 --> 00:04:29,910
which used to be the capital of the Isle of Man and its medieval castle.

65
00:04:29,910 --> 00:04:35,007
And on Day 6, it's back to the ferry or the airport

66
00:04:35,248 --> 00:04:39,000
if you flew to the island and time to go home

67
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,060
Now I'd like to tell you a bit more... (fade out)
